If UF provides fax machines for its students to use to send resumes to
local area employers, can UF discipline a student for using the
provided fax machine to send a political treatise to *every* fax
machine in the area?  And most of the relevant machines to the issue
are not owned by UF.  That is like saying that the only fax machines
relevant to the issue are owned by UF.  I have no problems with UF
being required to allow students to use their own machines, but like a
fax machine, whatever is posted to Usenet is automatically sent to use
resources elsewhere.  We do not say, "Well, the it is really okay
because it is really the fault of the fax machine for using the phone
system, and the fault of the phone system for passing the information
along to the other fax machine, and the fault of the fax machine for
automatically receiving the information."

