Yep you could do that, but your newsgroups line would probably get truncated
so that the news software could deal with it.  Break a lot of Waffle sites
too (though I think the Waffle people should fix this, software shouldn't
break on input like this).  Not to mention that with a newsgroups line of
several thousand newsgroups, no one would read it because it would take
too long to page past the newsgroups line.  Why do you think people spam
instead of making massive crossposts?

Check the history of alt.best.of.internet for an example of what happens 
when people claim the right to post wherever they damn well please.
Readers and posters leave, and newsgroups get ruined for their original
purpose.  I used to read alt.best.of.internet myself, but I left because
all off-topic posts made it no longer worth reading.
